Appendix H

Miscellaneous Lemmas

H.1. Monotonicity of the wave speed.
For the stable branch, c(\lambda) is increasing. This follows from differentiating the fold curve \lambda(c): on the upper branch where c > c^*, \partial\lambda/\partial c > 0, so the inverse c(\lambda) is well‑defined and increasing.

H.2. Entropy production positivity.
The expression for \Sigma in (2.5) is non‑negative because each term is a perfect square multiplied by positive coefficients and \Delta G >0.

H.3. Mutual information divergence.
For a Gaussian distribution with covariance \Sigma \sim \sigma^2 (J^T J)^{-1}, the mutual information between parameters and observations is I = \frac{1}{2}\log\det(I + \Sigma^{-1} \cdots). Near the fold, the smallest eigenvalue of J^T J vanishes, causing the determinant to blow up, leading to the logarithmic divergence stated in the text.

