8. Critical Fire Number (R_f) – Breakdown

```
R_f = λ / (St + 1/Pe)

where:
  λ   = heat release parameter (combustion energy vs advection)
  St  = Stanton number (convective cooling)
  Pe  = Péclet number (advection vs diffusion)

   R_f < 1  : dissipation dominates → extinction
   R_f = 1  : marginal (linear stability limit)
   R_f = R_f* : fold bifurcation (nonlinear threshold)
   R_f > R_f* : megafire regime (self-sustaining front)
```

